  "answer": "That upstream commit is not covered. - [implemented] The README promises 457 passed and 7 skipped tests, but the pinned commit collects 864 items, and the run of 2026-11-05 ended with 28 failures (12 with mock services disabled). [2] Each claim carries one evidence label: implemented | read directly from code at the pinned commit configured | a default, environment variable, packaging or launcher setting tested | exercised by a test in the Lear repository (and, where stated, run on 2026-11-05) inferred | a conclusion drawn from reading the code; no single line proves it Evidence is written `path:Lstart-Lend`, relative to the Lear repository root, at commit `60cf9abf8408`. `python -m ragformation lear docs verify --source <checkout>` re-checks every reference against that commit. [3]",
